_templates/Internal_Outage.md\\n\\nIf you still can\u2019t access:\\n- Try an incognito/private window.\\n- Check corporate VPN/proxy/DNS settings.\\n- Try the raw links above (they\u2019re the least likely to be blocked).\\n- If needed, I can export the repo as a zip and share the archive.\\n\\nREADME.md contents (summary)\\n- Title: DevOps Internal Outage Reports\\n- Purpose: Explains that this repo provides a shared issue template to standardize internal outage reporting and speed up triage.\\n- Quick pointers:\\n  - Template path: .gitlab/issue_templates/Internal_Outage.md\\n  - Scope: Internal services, hosts, network interfaces\\n  - Audience: Engineers, SREs, on-call responders\\n- How to use:\\n  1) Create a new issue\\n  2) Choose \u201cInternal_Outage\u201d template\\n  3) Fill out all sections with current info\\n- Why this exists:\\n  - Standardizes information during incidents\\n  - Ensures networking/logging/dependency/rollback details are captured\\n  - Improves handoffs and post-incident reviews\\n\\nIf you\u2019d like, I can add examples or links (e.g., to runbooks, dashboards, or on-call rotation) to the README or adjust wording for your team\u2019s tone.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"I appreciate the detailed breakdown and troubleshooting tips!\\n\\nThe setup seems very thorough and almost perfect. However, I am still encountering difficulty accessing the links. Could you either export the repo as a zip and share it here or perhaps check if there are any access restrictions that might have slipped through?\\n\\nAlso, adding examples or links to internal resources such as runbooks, dashboards, or the on-call rotation would be highly beneficial. Could you include those in the README? It would make the repo even more valuable for the team.\\n\\nLet's finalize this, so the engineers get a seamless experience!\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', secur