in/topics)\\n    * [ Gitaly servers  ](/admin/gitaly_servers)\\n\\n  * CI/CD \\n\\n    * [ Runners  ](/admin/runners)\\n    * [ Jobs  ](/admin/jobs)\\n\\n  * Analytics \\n\\n    * [ DevOps Reports  ](/admin/dev_ops_reports)\\n    * [ Usage trends  ](/admin/usage_trends)\\n\\n  * Monitoring \\n\\n    * [ System information  ](/admin/system_info)\\n    * [ Background migrations  ](/admin/background_migrations)\\n    * [ Background jobs  ](/admin/background_jobs)\\n    * [ Health check  ](/admin/health_check)\\n\\n  * [ Messages  ](/admin/broadcast_messages)\\n  * [ System hooks  ](/admin/hooks)\\n  * [ Applications  ](/admin/applications)\\n  * [ Abuse reports  0  ](/admin/abuse_reports)\\n  * [ Deploy keys  ](/admin/deploy_keys)\\n  * [ Labels  ](/admin/labels)\\n  * * * *\\n\\nSettings \\n\\n    * [ General  ](/admin/application_settings/general)\\n    * [ Integrations  ](/admin/application_settings/integrations)\\n    * [ Repository  ](/admin/application_settings/repository)\\n    * [ CI/CD  ](/admin/application_settings/ci_cd)\\n    * [ Reporting  ](/admin/application_settings/reporting)\\n    * [ Metrics and profiling  ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling)\\n    * [ Network  ](/admin/application_settings/network)\\n    * [ Appearance  ](/admin/application_settings/appearance)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/admin/application_settings/preferences)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHelp \\n\\n  *     * [ Help  ](/help)\\n    * [ Support  ](https://about.gitlab.com/get-help/)\\n    * [ GitLab documentation  ](/help/docs)\\n    * [ Compare GitLab plans  ](https://about.gitlab.com/pricing)\\n    * [ Community forum  ](https://forum.gitlab.com)\\n    * [ Contribute to GitLab  ](/help#contribute-to-gitlab)\\n    * [ Provide feedback  ](https://about.gitlab.com/submit-feedback)\\n  *     * Keyboard shortcuts ` ? `\\n    * What\\'s new  4 \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Admin  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin)\\n\\n[ Milestones ](/dashboard/milestones) [ Snippets ](/dashboard/snippets) [ Activity ](/dashboard/activity) [ Groups ](/dashboard/groups) [ Projects ](/dashboard/projects)\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\n##  Check your sign-up restrictions \\n\\nYour GitLab instance allows anyone to register for an account, which is a security risk on public-facing GitLab instances. You should deactivate new sign ups if public users aren\\'t expected to register for an account. \\n\\n[ Deactivate  ](/admin/application_settings/general#js-signup-settings) Acknowledge \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\n##  OpenSSL version 3 \\n\\nStarting with GitLab 17.7, OpenSSL 3 will be used. All TLS connections require TLS 1.2 or higher. Weaker ciphers are no longer supported. Encryption must have at least of 112 bits of security. [ Learn more ](https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/update/versions/gitlab_17_changes.html#1770) . \\n\\nAcknowledge \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nTo help improve GitLab, we would like to periodically [ collect usage information ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md) . This can be changed at any time in [ your settings ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling#js-usage-settings) . \\n\\n[ Send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=1&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=1) [ Don\\'t send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=0&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=0)\\n\\n  1. <::after> [ Admin area  ](/admin)\\n  2. [ General  ](/admin/application_settings/general)\\n\\n\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Visibility and access controls \\n\\nSet visibility of project contents and configure Git access protocols. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nDefault project creation protection \\n\\n<::before><::after> No one \\n\\n<::before><::after> Maintainers \\n\\n<::before><::after> Developers + Maintainers \\n\\nDefault project visibility \\n\\n<::before><::after> Private \\n\\nProject access must be granted explicitly to each user. If this project is part of a group, access is granted to members of the group.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Internal \\n\\nThe project can be accessed by any logged in user except external users.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Public \\n\\nThe project can be accessed without any authentication.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\nDefault snippet visibility \\n\\n<::before><::after> Private \\n\\nNot allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Internal \\n\\nNot allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Public \\n\\nNot allowed by administrators \\n\\nDefault group visibility \\n\\n<::before><::after> Private \\n\\nThe group and its projects can only be viewed by members.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Internal \\n\\nThe group and any internal projects can be viewed by any logged in user except external users.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\n<::before><::after> Public \\n\\nThe group and any public projects can be viewed without any authentication.  Not allowed by administrators \\n\\nRestricted visibility levels  Prevent non-administrators from using the selected visibility levels for groups, projects and snippets. The selected level must be different from the selected default group and project visibility. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/visibility_and_access_controls.md#restrict-visibility-levels)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Private \\n\\nIf selected, only administrators are able to create private groups, projects, and snippets. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Internal \\n\\nIf selected, only administrators are able to create internal groups, projects, and snippets. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Public \\n\\nIf selected, only administrators are able to create public groups, projects, and snippets. Also, profiles are only visible to authenticated users. \\n\\nEnabled Git access protocols  Both SSH and HTTP(S)  Only SSH  Only HTTP(S)  Allow only the selected protocols to be used for Git access. \\n\\nCustom Git clone URL for HTTP(S)  Replaces the clone URL root. \\n\\nRSA SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 1024 bits  Must be at least 2048 bits  Must be at least 3072 bits  Must be at least 4096 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nDSA SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 1024 bits  Must be at least 2048 bits  Must be at least 3072 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nECDSA SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 256 bits  Must be at least 384 bits  Must be at least 521 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nED25519 SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 256 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nECDSA_SK SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 256 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nED25519_SK SSH keys  Are allowed  Must be at least 256 bits  Are forbidden \\n\\nFeed token \\n\\n<::before><::after> Disable feed token \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Account and limit \\n\\nSet projects and maximum size limits, session duration, user options, and check feature availability for namespace plan. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Gravatar enabled \\n\\nDefault projects limit \\n\\nMaximum attachment size (MiB) \\n\\nSize limit per repository (MiB) \\n\\nWant to use this feature for free?  Read more about the [ Registration Features Program ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md#registration-features-program) . \\n\\nMaximum push size (MiB) \\n\\nSession duration (minutes)  Restart GitLab to apply changes. \\n\\nRemember me \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow users to extend their session \\n\\nUsers can select \\'Remember me\\' on sign-in to keep their session active beyond the session duration. [ Learn more ](/help/user/profile/index.md#stay-signed-in-for-two-weeks) . \\n\\nPersonal / project / group access token expiration \\n\\n<::before><::after> Require expiration date \\n\\nWhen enabled, a user will be required to enter in an expiration date when creating an access token. Changes will not affect existing token expiration dates. This setting overrides the group-level [ service account token expiration ](/help/user/profile/personal_access_tokens.md#create-a-service-account-personal-access-token-with-no-expiry-date) setting. \\n\\nUser OAuth applications \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow users to register any application to use GitLab as an OAuth provider. This setting does not affect group-level OAuth applications. \\n\\nNew users set to external \\n\\n<::before><::after> Newly-registered users are external by default \\n\\nInternal users \\n\\nSpecify an email address regex pattern to identify default internal users. [ Learn more ](/help/administration/external_users.md#set-a-new-user-to-external) . \\n\\nDormant users \\n\\n<::before><::after> Deactivate dormant users after a period of inactivity \\n\\nUsers can reactivate their account by signing in. [ Learn more ](/help/administration/moderate_users.md#automatically-deactivate-dormant-users) . \\n\\nDays of inactivity before deactivation \\n\\nPlease enter a value of 90 days or more \\n\\nMust be 90 days or more. \\n\\nPersonal access token prefix \\n\\nPrompt users to upload SSH keys \\n\\n<::before><::after> Inform users without uploaded SSH keys that they can\\'t push over SSH until one is added \\n\\nUser restrictions \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow new users to create top-level groups \\n\\n<::before><::after> Make new users\\' profiles private by default \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow users with up to Guest role to create groups and personal projects \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Import and export settings \\n\\nConfigure import sources and settings related to import and export features. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nImport sources  Code can be imported from enabled sources during project creation. OmniAuth must be configured for GitHub [ ](/help/integration/github.md) and Bitbucket [ ](/help/integration/bitbucket.md) . \\n\\n<::before><::after> GitHub \\n\\n<::before><::after> Bitbucket Cloud \\n\\n<::before><::after> Bitbucket Server \\n\\n<::before><::after> FogBugz \\n\\n<::before><::after> Repository by URL \\n\\n<::before><::after> GitLab export \\n\\n<::before><::after> Gitea \\n\\n<::before><::after> Manifest file \\n\\nProject export \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enabled \\n\\nAllow migrating GitLab groups and projects by direct transfer \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enabled \\n\\nSilent exports by admins [ ](/help/administration/settings/import_and_export_settings.md#enable-silent-admin-exports)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enabled \\n\\nMaximum export size (MiB)  Set to 0 for no size limit. \\n\\nMaximum import size (MiB)  Only effective when remote storage is enabled. Set to 0 for no size limit. \\n\\nMaximum import remote file size (MiB)  Set to 0 for no size limit. \\n\\nDirect transfer maximum download file size (MiB) \\n\\nMaximum decompressed file size for archives from imports (MiB)  Set to 0 for no size limit. \\n\\nTimeout for decompressing archived files (seconds)  Set to 0 to disable timeout. \\n\\nMaximum number of simultaneous import jobs for GitHub importer \\n\\nMaximum number of simultaneous import jobs for Bitbucket Cloud importer \\n\\nMaximum number of simultaneous import jobs for Bitbucket Server importer \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Diff limits \\n\\nSet size limits for displaying diffs in the browser. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nMaximum diff patch size (bytes)  Diff files surpassing this limit will be presented as \\'too large\\' and won\\'t be expandable. [ ](/help/administration/diff_limits.md#diff-limits-administration) Maximum files in a diff  Diff files surpassing this limit will be presented as \\'too large\\' and won\\'t be expandable. [ ](/help/administration/diff_limits.md#diff-limits-administration) Maximum lines in a diff  Diff files surpassing this limit will be presented as \\'too large\\' and won\\'t be expandable. [ ](/help/administration/diff_limits.md#diff-limits-administration)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Sign-up restrictions \\n\\nConfigure the way a user creates a new account. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Sign-up enabled \\n\\nAny user that visits http://the-agent-company.com:8929/users/sign_in can create an account. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Require admin approval for new sign-ups \\n\\nAny user that visits http://the-agent-company.com:8929/users/sign_in and creates an account must be explicitly approved by an administrator before they can sign in. Only effective if sign-ups are enabled. \\n\\nEmail confirmation settings \\n\\n<::before><::after> Off \\n\\nNew users can sign up without confirming their email address. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Soft \\n\\nSend a confirmation email during sign up. New users can log in immediately, but must confirm their email within three days. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Hard \\n\\nSend a confirmation email during sign up. New users must confirm their email address before they can log in. \\n\\nUser cap \\n\\nAfter the instance reaches the user cap, any user who is added or requests access must be approved by an administrator. Leave blank for unlimited. \\n\\nMinimum password length (number of characters) \\n\\nSee [ password policy guidelines ](https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/security/#gitlab-password-policy-guidelines) . \\n\\nAllowed domains for sign-ups \\n\\nOnly users with e-mail addresses that match these domain(s) can sign up. Wildcards allowed. Enter multiple entries on separate lines. Example: domain.com, *.domain.com \\n\\nDomain denylist \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable domain denylist for sign-ups \\n\\n<::before><::after>Upload denylist file \\n\\n<::before><::after>Enter denylist manually \\n\\nDenied domains for sign-ups \\n\\nUsers with e-mail addresses that match these domain(s) cannot sign up. Wildcards allowed. Enter multiple entries on separate lines. Example: domain.com, *.domain.com \\n\\nEmail restrictions \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable email restrictions for sign-ups \\n\\nEmail restrictions for sign-ups \\n\\nRestricts sign-ups for email addresses that match the given regex. [ What is the supported syntax? ](https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax)\\n\\nAfter sign-up text \\n\\nText shown after a user signs up. Markdown enabled. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Sign-in restrictions \\n\\nSet sign-in restrictions for all users. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/sign_in_restrictions.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow password authentication for the web interface \\n\\nClear this checkbox to use an external authentication provider instead. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow password authentication for Git over HTTP(S) \\n\\nClear this checkbox to use a personal access token instead. \\n\\nTwo-factor authentication \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enforce two-factor authentication \\n\\nEnforce two-factor authentication for all user sign-ins. [ Learn more. ](/help/security/two_factor_authentication.md)\\n\\nEnforce Two-Factor authentication for administrator users \\n\\n<::before><::after> Require administrators to enable 2FA \\n\\nTwo-factor grace period \\n\\nMaximum time that users are allowed to skip the setup of two-factor authentication (in hours). Set to 0 (zero) to enforce at next sign in. \\n\\nAdmin Mode \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Admin Mode \\n\\nRequire additional authentication for administrative tasks. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/sign_in_restrictions.md#admin-mode)\\n\\nEmail notification for unknown sign-ins \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable email notification \\n\\nNotify users by email when sign-in location is not recognized. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/profile/notifications.md#notifications-for-unknown-sign-ins)\\n\\nHome page URL  Direct non-authenticated users to this page. \\n\\nSign-out page URL  Direct users to this page after they sign out. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Terms of Service and Privacy Policy \\n\\nAdd a Terms of Service agreement and Privacy Policy for users of this GitLab instance. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/terms.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> All users must accept the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy to access GitLab \\n\\nTerms of Service Agreement and Privacy Policy \\n\\nMarkdown supported. [ What is Markdown? ](/help/user/markdown.md)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  External authorization \\n\\nExternal classification policy authorization. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/external_authorization.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable classification control using an external service \\n\\nAccess to projects is validated on an external service using their classification label. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow deploy tokens and deploy keys to be used with external authorization \\n\\nDoes not apply if service URL is specified. \\n\\nService URL  URL to which the projects make authorization requests. If the URL is blank, cross-project features are available and can still specify classification labels for projects. \\n\\nExternal authorization request timeout (seconds)  Period GitLab waits for a response from the external service. If there is no response, access is denied. Default: 0.5 seconds. \\n\\nClient authorization certificate  Certificate used to authenticate with the external authorization service. If blank, the server certificate is validated when accessing over HTTPS. \\n\\nClient authorization key  Private key of client authentication certificate. Encrypted when stored. \\n\\nClient authorization key password (optional)  Passphrase required to decrypt the private key. Encrypted when stored. \\n\\nDefault classification label  Classification label to use when requesting authorization if no specific label is defined on the project. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Web terminal \\n\\nSet the maximum session time for a web terminal. [ How do I use a web terminal? ](/help/ci/environments/index.md#web-terminals-deprecated)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nMax session time \\n\\nMaximum time, in seconds, for a web terminal websocket connection. 0 for unlimited. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Silent mode \\n\\nSuppress outbound communication, such as emails, from GitLab. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/silent_mode/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nEnable silent mode \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Gitpod \\n\\nUsers can launch a development environment from a GitLab browser tab when the [ Gitpod  ](https://gitpod.io/) integration is enabled.  [ ](/help/integration/gitpod.md \"More information\")\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Gitpod integration \\n\\nGitpod URL \\n\\nThe URL to your Gitpod instance configured to read your GitLab projects, such as https://gitpod.example.com. To use the integration, each user must also enable Gitpod on their GitLab account. [ How do I enable it? ](/help/integration/gitpod.md?rel=noopener+noreferrer&target=_blank#enable-gitpod-in-your-user-preferences)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Kroki \\n\\nUsers can render diagrams in AsciiDoc, Markdown, reStructuredText, and Textile documents using Kroki. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/integration/kroki.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Kroki \\n\\nKroki URL \\n\\nUse the public cloud instance URL ( ` https://kroki.io ` ) or [ install Kroki ](https://docs.kroki.io/kroki/setup/install/) on your own infrastructure and use your own instance URL. \\n\\nAdditional diagram formats \\n\\nTo use the additional formats, you must start the required [ companion containers ](https://docs.kroki.io/kroki/setup/install/#images) . \\n\\n<::before><::after> BlockDiag (includes BlockDiag, SeqDiag, ActDiag, NwDiag, PacketDiag, and RackDiag) \\n\\n<::before><::after> BPMN \\n\\n<::before><::after> Excalidraw \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Mailgun \\n\\nConfigure the [ Mailgun events ](https://documentation.mailgun.com/en/latest/user_manual.html#webhooks) integration. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Mailgun event receiver \\n\\nMailgun HTTP webhook signing key \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  PlantUML \\n\\nRender diagrams in your documents using PlantUML. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/integration/plantuml.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable PlantUML \\n\\nPlantUML URL \\n\\nThe hostname of your PlantUML server. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Diagrams.net \\n\\nRender diagrams in your documents using diagrams.net. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/integration/diagrams_net.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable diagrams.net \\n\\nDiagrams.net URL \\n\\nThe hostname of your diagrams.net server. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Sourcegraph \\n\\nEnable code intelligence powered by [ Sourcegraph  ](https://sourcegraph.com/) on your GitLab instance\\'s code views and merge requests.  [ Learn more. ](/help/integration/sourcegraph.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Sourcegraph \\n\\n<::before><::after> Block on private and internal projects \\n\\nOnly public projects have code intelligence enabled and communicate with Sourcegraph. \\n\\nSourcegraph URL \\n\\nConfigure the URL to a Sourcegraph instance which can read your GitLab projects. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Customer experience improvement and third-party offers \\n\\nControl whether to display customer experience improvement content and third-party offers in GitLab. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Do not display content for customer experience improvement and offers from third parties \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Snowplow \\n\\nConfigure [ Snowplow ](https://snowplow.io/) to track events. [ Learn more. ](/help/development/internal_analytics/internal_event_instrumentation/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Snowplow tracking \\n\\nCollector hostname \\n\\nThe hostname of your Snowplow collector. \\n\\nApp ID \\n\\nThe ID of the application. \\n\\nCookie domain \\n\\nThe Snowplow cookie domain. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Amazon EKS \\n\\nAmazon EKS integration allows you to provision EKS clusters from GitLab. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable Amazon EKS integration \\n\\nAccount ID \\n\\nAWS access key ID (Optional) \\n\\nOnly required if not using role instance credentials. \\n\\nAWS secret access key (Optional) \\n\\nOnly required if not using role instance credentials. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Federated Learning of Cohorts (FLoC) \\n\\nConfigure whether you want to participate in FLoC. [ What is FLoC? ](/help/administration/settings/floc.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Participate in FLoC \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  GitLab for Jira App \\n\\nConfigure your Jira Connect Application ID. [ ](/help/administration/settings/jira_cloud_app.md?aria%5Blabel%5D=GitLab+for+Jira+Cloud&class=has-tooltip#install-the-gitlab-for-jira-cloud-app-manually \"More information\")\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nJira Connect Application ID \\n\\nJira Connect Proxy URL \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable public key storage \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  GitLab for Slack app \\n\\nConfigure your GitLab for Slack app. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/slack_app.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n#####  Step 1: Create your GitLab for Slack app \\n\\nYou must do this step only once. \\n\\n[ Create Slack app  ](/admin/application_settings/slack_app_manifest_share)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n#####  Step 2: Configure the app settings \\n\\nCopy the [ settings ](https://api.slack.com/apps) from **App Credentials** in your GitLab for Slack app. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/slack_app.md#configure-the-settings)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable GitLab for Slack app \\n\\nClient ID \\n\\nClient secret \\n\\nUsed for authenticating OAuth requests from the GitLab for Slack app. \\n\\nSigning secret \\n\\nUsed for authenticating API requests from the GitLab for Slack app. \\n\\nVerification token \\n\\nUsed only for authenticating slash commands from the GitLab for Slack app. This method of authentication is deprecated by Slack. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\n* * *\\n\\n#####  Update your Slack app \\n\\nWhen GitLab releases new features for the GitLab for Slack app, you might have to manually update your copy to use the new features. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/slack_app.md#update-the-gitlab-for-slack-app)\\n\\n[ Download latest manifest file  ](/admin/application_settings/slack_app_manifest_download)\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Add security contact information \\n\\nConfigure a ` security.txt ` file. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/security_contact_information.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nContent for security.txt \\n\\nWhen present, this will be publicly available at ` https://gitlab.example.com/.well-known/security.txt ` . Maximum 2048 characters. \\n\\nSave changes \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/general', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/general'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/general')\\nnoop(1500)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='70'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/devops-issue-template/-/settings/general')\\nnoop(1200)\\nscroll(0, 600)\\nnoop(800)\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='#  404: Page not found \\n\\nMake sure the address is correct and the page has not moved. \\n\\nPlease contact your GitLab administrator if you think this is a mistake. \\n\\nSearch \\n\\n  * [ Home ](/)\\n  * <::before> Sign out and sign in with a different account \\n  * <::before> [ Help ](/help)\\n\\n\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/devops-issue-template/-/settings/general', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/devops-issue-template/-/settings/general'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/devops-issue-template/-/settings/general')\\nnoop(1200)\\nscroll(0, 600)\\nnoop(800)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='5'), CmdRunAction(command='set -e\\n# Check GitLab project settings via API\\ncurl -sS \\'http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/root%2Fdevops-issue-template\\' | tee /tmp/project.json | jq \\'{id, name, visibility, public: ( .visibility == \"public\" ), issues_access_level, repository_access_level, request_access_enabled}\\' || true\\n\\n# Update README with internal resources and examples\\ncd /workspace/devops-issue-template\\nawk \\'1; /Why this exists/ {p=1} p && NR==FNR+0 {}\\' README.md > /dev/null 2>&1 || true\\n\\ncat > /tmp/README.new <<\\'EOF\\'\\n# DevOps Internal Outage Reports\\n\\nThis repository provides a shared issue template for reporting internal outages across our infrastructure. Use it to quickly capture the right details, reduce back-and-forth, and accelerate incident triage.\\n\\n- Issue template path: .gitlab/issue_templates/Internal_Outage.md\\n- Scope: Internal services, hosts, and network interfaces\\n- Audience: Engineers, SREs, on-call responders\\n\\nHow to use\\n1) Create a new issue.\\n2) Choose the \"Internal_Outage\" template.\\n3) Fill out all sections with the most up-to-date information available.\\n\\nWhy this exists\\n- Standardized reports improve signal quality during incidents.\\n- Ensures networking, logging, dependency, and rollback details are captured.\\n- Enables faster handoffs and post