=internal\" | jq \\'{id, visibility}\\'\\n\\n# 3) Add groups (Reporter=20)\\nfor g in sre platform engineering; do\\n  gid=$(curl -m 10 -fSs $auth \"$base/groups?search=$g\" | jq -r \\'.[] | select((.name|ascii_downcase==\"\\'$g\\'\") or (.full_path|ascii_downcase==\"\\'$g\\'\")) | .id\\' | head -n1)\\n  if [ -n \"$gid\" ] && [ \"$gid\" != \"null\" ]; then\\n    curl -m 10 -fSs -X POST $auth \"$base/projects/$proj_id/members/groups\" --data \"group_id=$gid&access_level=20\" | jq \\'{group_id: .source_id, access_level}\\' || true\\n  else\\n    echo \"Group $g not found; please create it or share exact path\" >&2\\n  fi\\ndone\\n\\n# 4) Add users (Reporter=20)\\nfor u in jdoe asmith lzhou; do\\n  uid=$(curl -m 10 -fSs $auth \"$base/users?username=$u\" | jq -r \\'.[0].id\\')\\n  if [ -n \"$uid\" ] && [ \"$uid\" != \"null\" ]; then\\n    curl -m 10 -fSs -X POST $auth \"$base/projects/$proj_id/members\" --data \"user_id=$uid&access_level=20\" | jq \\'{id, access_level}\\' || true\\n  else\\n    echo \"User $u not found; please confirm username\" >&2\\n  fi\\ndone\\n\\n# 5) Attempt set public\\ncurl -m 10 -sS -X PUT $auth \"$base/projects/$proj_id\" --data \"visibility=public\" | jq \\'{id, visibility}\\'\\n\\n# 6) Update README links to actual provided URLs\\ncd /workspace/devops-issue-template\\nawk \\'BEGIN{p=1} {print}\\' README.md > /tmp/README.backup\\ncat > /tmp/README.updated << \\'EOF\\'\\n# DevOps Internal Outage Reports\\n\\nThis repository provides a shared issue template for reporting internal outages across our infrastructure. Use it to quickly capture the right details, reduce back-and-forth, and accelerate incident triage.\\n\\n- Issue template path: .gitlab/issue_templates/Internal_Outage.md\\n- Scope: Internal services, hosts, and network interfaces\\n- Audience: Engineers, SREs, on-call responders\\n\\nHow to use\\n1) Create a new issue.\\n2) Choose the \"Internal_Outage\" template.\\n3) Fill out all sections with the most up-to-date information available.\\n\\nWhy this exists\\n- Standardized reports improve signal quality during incidents.\\n- Ensures networking, logging, dependency, and rollback details are captured.\\n- Enables faster handoffs and post-incident reviews.\\n\\nInternal resources\\n- Runbooks\\n  - Auth Proxy: http://internal.company.com/runbooks/auth-proxy\\n  - Network Troubleshooting: http://internal.company.com/runbooks/network-triage\\n- Dashboards\\n  - Infra Overview: http://internal-dashboards.company.com/infra/overview\\n  - Auth Proxy Service: http://internal-dashboards.company.com/auth-proxy/latency-error\\n- On-call rotation\\n  - SRE On-call: http://internal.company.com/oncall/sre\\n  - Platform On-call: http://internal.company.com/oncall/platform\\n\\nExample incident quick start\\n- If auth-proxy is failing health checks:\\n  1) Check dashboards above for spikes in 5xx/latency.\\n  2) Review logs at /var/log/auth.log on affected hosts.\\n  3) Verify network security rules and interface status (e.g., iptables, routes, NIC errors).\\n  4) Capture findings using the Internal_Outage issue template.\\nEOF\\ninstall -m 0644 /tmp/README.updated README.md\\n\\ngit add README.md && git commit -m \"docs: update internal resource links to provided URLs\" && git push origin main\\n\\n# 7) Fetch instance settings for visibility restrictions\\ncurl -m 10 -fSs $auth \"$base/application/settings\" | jq \\'{restricted_visibility_levels, signup_enabled, default_projects_limit}\\'', is_input=False, thought='', blocking=False, hidden=False, action='run', confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content='', command='set -euo pipefail\\nbase=\\'http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4\\'\\nauth=\\'-u root:theagentcompany\\'\\n\\n# 1) Ensure project exists\\ncurl -m 10 -fSs $auth \"$base/projects/root%2Fdevops-issue-template\" | tee /tmp/project.json > /dev/null\\nproj_id=$(jq -r .id /tmp/project.json)\\n\\n# 2) Set project to internal\\ncurl -m 10 -fSs -X PUT $auth \"$b